content.text:
verdict: clean
scenario_results:
  - {scenario: 1, result: pass, notes: "name, description, tools, maxTurns precede type/id/owner; nothing external is required to fill the seat (the reconcile-and-close link is a skill reference, not a missing input); 'You hold the shape seat' commits to no actor kind, and the authority-set threshold is stated once with a default until set."}
  - {scenario: 2, result: pass, notes: "No sentence says when the seat acts; interface arrows ('framed intent arrives, feasibility and shape return') describe direction, not order, and 'before a change' is part of the pre-state definition, not a step."}
  - {scenario: 3, result: pass, notes: "One claim: 'Domain (exclusive): the stack — which technologies the product is built on is decided by this seat alone.' Decision-phrased; Decides-list items are rights, not labeled exclusive."}
  - {scenario: 4, result: pass, notes: "Six bullets, each an artifact or judgment checkable after a run (structural model artifact, ADRs, recorded decomposition, scenario mapping, register reconciliation, clarify answers); no trait bullets."}
  - {scenario: 5, result: pass, notes: "Seat writes ADRs/artifacts so Read/Edit/Write/Bash fit; drift-prone judgment seat carries maxTurns: 60; 'never from its internals' and 'bounds, never approves' have no mechanical enforcement in a frontmatter key, so nothing enforceable is left unenforced."}
stumbles: ["published package data — the evidence class is decidable only by contrast with 'a local copy of published data'; a reader must infer it means registry/upstream metadata", "the seat's value is inversely proportional to the number of decisions it makes — rhetorical, not a rule a reviewer can score"]
top_changes: ["Name what 'published package data' is (e.g. upstream registry metadata) in one clause so the admissible-evidence line is decidable without inference", "Replace the inverse-proportion sentence with the plain rule already implied: decide only what is hard to reverse; bound everything else"]
